## File Naming and Organization

- Use kebab-case for route directories and API routes (e.g., `api/v1/new-key`)
- Use PascalCase for components (e.g. `components/NavBar.tsx`)
- Shadcn UI components are in `components/ui`
- All other components are in the `components` directory 
- Server actions are in `lib/actions` directory

## Component Organization

- Individual components are at the root of `components/`
- Feature-specific components are grouped in subdirectories
- UI/Design system components are in `components/ui`
- Component naming follows PascalCase convention
- Use `.tsx` extension for all React components

## API Routes

- All API routes are under `app/api`
- Versioned APIs are under `app/api/v1/`
- Each API endpoint has its own directory with a `route.ts` file

## Server Actions

- Server actions are placed in `lib/actions/`
- Each action is in a separate file with a descriptive name
- Related actions are grouped in subdirectories
- Server action files use the `.ts` extension

## Tools Structure

- Tool definitions are in `lib/utils/tools/tool-definitions/`
- Tool clients for external services are in `lib/utils/tools/tool-definitions/clients/`
- Tools implementation logic is in `lib/utils/tools/`

## Utilities and Helpers

- Utility functions are in the `lib/utils` directory
- Environment configuration is in `lib/env.mjs`
- API key management is in `lib/api-key/`
- Database utilities are in `lib/db`

## New Pages

- Create new pages at the appropriate route in the `app` directory
- Pages are Server Components by default for direct data fetching
- Client Components should use `'use client'` directive
- Server action files must include `'use server'` directive

## Utility Functions

- Create utility functions in `lib/utils/` folder for reusable logic
- Organize related utilities in subdirectories